Session: Supervisor. **This issue takes over from #516**, which has reached GitHub's limit of 2,500 comments and can no longer be commented on (2026-11-07, 06:00 UTC).

Everything that went on #516 goes here from now on. Anywhere CLAUDE.md, a scheduled round or an earlier comment says "#516", read this issue. Older history stays on #516.
- RepoManager's round reports.
- Supervisor's merge lists, which are standing instructions.
- Deploy handovers to dev1.
- "<role> online, session <id>" notes.
- Catch-up and process rules.

**Standing instructions carried over from #516:**
1. **The catch-up rules** (owner, 2026-11-07):
   - batches by default, up to six, merged in order with the merge method; split a failed batch in half;
   - no refresh when the CI areas don't overlap;
   - refresh only what merges next;
   - no new PR from a session with 4 or more open non-draft PRs (owner-urgent fixes and log-only PRs excepted);
   - RepoManager subscribes to PR activity on approved PRs.
2. **Merge order:** Supervisor's audit list of 05:58 UTC on #516: https://github.com/smv620/Discord-DMbot/issues/516#issuecomment-6703078451. Updates:
   - #3575, #3594, #3600, #3587 and #3638 are re-approved on their current heads;
   - #3719 is approved;
   - #3380 and #3589 are back with CloudDev-lead.
3. **Deploys:** step 9 is live (dev1's log, #3689). The next handover comes here once `development` is green on one exact commit. dev1's open checks are on #3328.

## Parents

- #207 `MVP: Reusable zero-paid local CI host for private repositories`
- #195 `Enforcement: require deterministic policy gate for operator-facing commands`

## Precondition

PR #214 / Issue #213 completed the final non-live owner-machine/JIT bridge plan on current `main`.

Merged baseline at child-issue creation:

`0b0508d4f6ad2765e315e39450b71adfb371f8ca`

PR #214 final reviewed head:

`ce9953e754a642fba3700ef1ec94d6782badda15`

The non-live plan reached planning authority only. It did not register a runner, dispatch a workflow, mutate the HP ProDesk, or execute target repository code.

This child issue is the **first live pilot**. Live effects remain human-authorized and must occur only after deterministic preflight/gate evidence is complete.

## Goal

Execute exactly one repository-scoped JIT/ephemeral Windows runner job on the dedicated HP ProDesk for one explicitly selected private repository, under a separate non-admin target execution identity, then prove teardown/reset and zero residual authority.

Success may produce only:

`SELF_HOSTED_PRIVATE_CI_PASS`

for the exact repository / PR / SHA / workflow / runner nonce / environment generation used by this pilot.

It must not be relabeled as `GITHUB_HOSTED_CI_PASS`.

Public `oimus1976/agent-controller` remains GitHub-hosted only.

## Human-final boundary

This issue does not pre-authorize live owner-machine/GitHub mutation merely by existing.

Before the first live effect, Controller must present one exact human action/gate bound to the frozen pilot identity and current authoritative evidence.

Human authorization is required before any operation that actually:

- registers/deregisters the repository-scoped runner;
- creates/deletes/resets a local execution account/profile if required by the frozen plan;
- mutates local group/ACL/service/task state;
- obtains/uses a real one-time runner registration/JIT credential;
- dispatches the trusted private-repository workflow;
- executes target repository code on the owner machine.

Ready/merge remain human-final under ADR #90 and are unrelated to pilot PASS.

## Pilot target selection

Before mutation, freeze exactly one selected private repository and one open same-repository Draft PR with:

- repository full name;
- `visibility = private` from fresh GitHub evidence;
- PR number;
- exact current 40-hex PR head SHA;
- expected base/default branch relationship;
- trusted workflow identity/version from the default branch;
- target OS/runtime = Windows;
- repository-scoped runner registration scope;
- fresh one-time runner nonce and canonical unique label;
- execution-environment generation/reset identity;
- trusted broker/admin identity;
- separate non-admin target identity;
- authoritative evidence root `C:\Users\Public\Documents\agent-controller-handoff`.

Do not select public repositories, fork-head PRs, closed/merged PRs, arbitrary branches/SHAs, or targets with uncertain workflow/head state.

The exact target repository/PR is an operator decision at pilot start and must be frozen before any live capability is acquired.

## Required phase order

The pilot must be fail-fast and ordered. Later phases cannot run after an earlier required phase fails or becomes uncertain.

### Phase 0 — fresh source-of-truth preflight

Fresh-read and prove:

- `agent-controller` current `main` still contains the accepted non-live bridge/gate implementation;
- no conflicting active workstream/writer invalidates the target;
- selected repository remains private;
- PR remains open, Draft, same-repository head;
- exact head SHA equals the frozen expected SHA;
- trusted workflow identity/version is exact;
- no unexpected runner with the pilot label/nonce is already registered;
- execution environment/reset baseline is acceptable;
- required identities/runtime/tool paths are present;
- no stale pilot authority/capability is being reused.

Any mismatch -> STOP before mutation.

### Phase 1 — deterministic operator-step gate

Render the first live operator command only from the frozen pilot contract and validate it through the merged #195/#213 authority path.

Requirements include:

- Windows PowerShell 5.1 compatible;
- candidate/spec digests exact;
- authenticated AST/effect attestation valid;
- exact repo/PR/SHA/host/identity/evidence-root bindings;
- no `$args` / `$Args` custom variable/parameter use;
- no unresolved placeholders;
- effect set is exactly the phase-authorized mutation set;
- required prior evidence/capability is fresh and one-time;
- heartbeat/progress, child exit-code, fail-fast, transcript and final-result requirements are present where applicable.

Gate outcome must be `PASS_TO_OPERATOR` before the command may be presented as the live next step.

### Phase 2 — human authorization for first live effect

Stop and present the exact bound action to the human.

Do not infer authorization from issue creation, chat continuation, elapsed time, or previous pilot approvals.

After the human performs/authorizes the exact action, Controller must re-observe authoritative local/GitHub state rather than trusting prose.

### Phase 3 — repository-scoped JIT/ephemeral registration

Acquire/use only a repository-scoped one-job/JIT-or-equivalent runner configuration for the selected private repository.

Requirements:

- fresh unique nonce/label;
- no default reusable runner authority;
- target identity cannot read broker GitHub auth, registration credential, AST/HMAC keys, or durable-authority DB/write capability;
- runner registration credential is treated as one-time/high-sensitivity material and removed from target reach before target code executes;
- registration result is independently read back from GitHub.

Unexpected/stale/duplicate registration -> STOP and enter cleanup/reconciliation; do not dispatch target code.

### Phase 4 — target environment preparation

Prepare the non-admin target environment exactly as planned.

Before target checkout/execution prove:

- target identity is not admin/broker identity;
- broker/provider/personal credentials are absent from target-readable locations;
- repository workspace belongs to the frozen environment generation;
- no prior repository checkout, secrets, caches, process state, or cross-repository state is inherited unless explicitly allowlisted by the frozen contract;
- junction/reparse containment requirements remain satisfied;
- credential handoff/removal semantics are proven by actual runtime behavior where applicable, not merely inferred from ACL masks.

This phase must preserve lessons from #201 real credential-deletion failure: an ACL-shaped PASS is not enough if the required one-time credential lifecycle operation cannot actually succeed.

### Phase 5 — exactly one job

Launch/allow exactly one job for the frozen repository/PR/SHA/workflow/nonce.

Target execution must:

- checkout the exact frozen SHA;
- use `clean: true` / equivalent clean checkout semantics;
- not persist GitHub checkout credentials to target code unless explicitly required and separately justified;
- run only the trusted default-branch workflow contract for this pilot;
- capture actual child/process/job exit status and required test results;
- expose progress or bounded heartbeat;
- stop immediately on non-zero required phase result;
- never emit `SELF_HOSTED_PRIVATE_CI_PASS` after a failed phase.

No second job is permitted under the same pilot authority.

### Phase 6 — teardown/reset

After target execution, whether PASS or FAIL, execute the frozen cleanup/reset plan before any reuse.

At minimum:

- stop/remove the one-job runner process/state;
- remove/revoke one-time registration/JIT material;
- destroy or deterministically reset the target execution environment/profile according to the frozen generation policy;
- remove target checkout/workspace and sensitive one-time files as required;
- ensure no target process/service/task remains;
- preserve authoritative transcripts/evidence before destructive cleanup of ephemeral state.

Cleanup failure does not erase the target job result, but it blocks pilot PASS/reuse.

Do not perform unrelated retained fixture/worktree cleanup without separate authorization.

### Phase 7 — authoritative zero-residual readback

Fresh-read both GitHub and local state after teardown.

Require zero residual authority for the frozen pilot identity, including as applicable:

- no registered runner for the nonce/label;
- no queued/in-progress job that can still target it;
- no reusable registration credential;
- no stale runner service/process;
- no residual target credential/authority material;
- reset generation reaches the expected terminal state;
- exact target PR/head remains identifiable and no unrelated ref mutation occurred.

Unknown/missing/unreadable post-state -> FAIL/BLOCKED, never PASS.

## Evidence contract

Persist authoritative pilot evidence under:

`C:\Users\Public\Documents\agent-controller-handoff`

Evidence must bind at least:

- pilot operation/workstream id;
- selected repository and visibility observation;
- PR number + exact target SHA;
- workflow identity/version;
- host + broker/target identity;
- nonce/runner label;
- environment generation;
- operator-step spec/candidate digests and gate result;
- human-gate boundary/action identity without recording secrets;
- registration readback;
- target execution start/end/result and actual exit/job status;
- teardown/reset result;
- GitHub/local zero-residual post-read;
- final classification.

Do not store runner registration tokens, GitHub tokens, passwords, HMAC keys, or other reusable credentials in Git/GitHub evidence.

## PASS rule

Emit `SELF_HOSTED_PRIVATE_CI_PASS` exactly once and only if all required conditions pass:

1. frozen target remained exact through execution;
2. one-job target execution completed successfully;
3. required tests/checks passed;
4. teardown/reset completed successfully;
5. authoritative GitHub/local post-read proves zero residual runner/authority/environment state required by the contract;
6. evidence is complete and bound to the same pilot identity.

Target test success alone is insufficient.

Cleanup success without target success is insufficient.

Console text alone is insufficient.

Any `FAIL`, `BLOCKED`, or `UNCERTAIN` phase prevents final PASS.

## Failure handling

On failure:

- stop subsequent normal phases immediately except required safety cleanup/reconciliation;
- preserve transcript/evidence;
- do not silently retry registration, dispatch, target execution, or cleanup;
- do not reuse nonce/label/one-time credential;
- do not create another live pilot automatically;
- classify whether failure is target-code failure, harness/gate failure, registration/runtime failure, or cleanup/post-read failure;
- any next live attempt requires a fresh issue/explicitly authorized retry or an explicit update to this issue after the failure is understood.

## Explicit non-goals

- enabling self-hosted execution for public `agent-controller`;
- multiple repository pilots in one authority grant;
- multiple jobs under one runner/nonce;
- unattended automatic retry;
- automatic Ready/merge;
- auto-purchase/provider-capacity changes;
- Linux/Ubuntu equivalence proof in this Windows pilot;
- generic daemon/scheduler/autoscaler;
- broad owner-machine administration beyond the exact pilot effects.

## Acceptance criteria

1. One exact private repository + open same-repo Draft PR + exact SHA is frozen before live mutation.
2. Fresh GitHub/local preflight proves target and baseline state; uncertainty blocks mutation.
3. Every operator-facing live command passes the deterministic #195/#213 gate before presentation/execution.
4. The first live effect stops at a precise human authorization boundary.
5. Runner registration is repository-scoped and one-job/JIT-or-equivalent with a fresh unique nonce/label.
6. Target code runs only under the separate non-admin target identity and cannot read broker/registration/controller authority credentials.
7. Actual one-time credential/read-delete lifecycle behavior is verified where used; ACL shape alone is not treated as runtime proof.
8. Exactly one job executes for the frozen repository/PR/SHA/workflow/nonce.
9. Progress/heartbeat, actual process/job status, fail-fast phase ordering, and durable transcript requirements are satisfied.
10. Any required execution failure prevents final PASS and prevents later normal phases except safety cleanup/reconciliation.
11. Teardown/reset runs after target execution and is itself fail-closed.
12. Fresh GitHub/local post-read proves zero residual runner/queued authority/credential/environment state required by the contract.
13. `SELF_HOSTED_PRIVATE_CI_PASS` is emitted only after target success + cleanup success + zero-residual readback; it is never called GitHub-hosted CI.
14. Public `agent-controller` remains GitHub-hosted only.
15. A failed/uncertain pilot is not automatically retried and no nonce/one-time credential is reused.
16. Ready/merge and other ADR #90 human-final actions remain unchanged.
17. Authoritative evidence is retained at the established handoff root and contains no reusable secrets.
18. Pilot closeout records the exact final outcome back to #207/#195 without claiming broader multi-repository production readiness from one run.

## Execution order

Follow:

`fresh preflight -> deterministic gate -> human live authorization -> registration -> environment prep -> exactly one job -> teardown/reset -> zero-residual readback -> classify`

Do not execute any live mutation merely because this issue was created.

At pilot start, re-read current `main`, open PR/WIP state, target private-repository state, and the exact operator-step evidence before asking the human for the first live action.

Use `Refs #207` / `Refs #195`; this pilot does not close either parent by itself.

Workstream: `private-local-ci-host`.
